       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't address the problem: 50 mg is five times the maximum labeled daily dose of amlodipine, and I don't know of an indication for that dose in an adult with normal kidney and liver function. At that dose the main risk is severe hypotension, and the drug has a long half-life, so the effect would last. Please check the dose with the prescriber or pharmacy before it goes in.\n\nHere are the options I can enter:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily**, a common starting dose.\n- Another dose within the labeled range (2.5 to 10 mg), if you tell me which one.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for 50 mg that I'm not aware of, you can enter that order directly in the order-entry system so that it goes through your normal verification and pharmacist review."
